T3,T4) + (T3,T4,T5) impossible due to T4 conflict.  \nOption 2: (T2,T3,T4) + (T3,T3,T3) as pung, not chow.  \n\nGiven remaining tiles, making pung of T3 is possible (4 unshown T3 left, I have 2 T3, so need 1 more T3).  \n\nAlso B3: I have B3\u00d72, so B3 pung possible (4 unshown B3 left).  \n\nIf I aim for:  \nMeld 1: W2,W3,W4 (already)  \nMeld 2: W7,W8,W9 (already)  \nMeld 3: T2,T3,T4 (in hand)  \nMeld 4: B3,B3,B3 (need one more B3)  \nPair: B7,B7 (need one more B7)  \n\nThat gives waiting on B7 for pair and B3 for pung.  \n\nAlternate:  \nMeld 3: T3,T3,T3 (need one more T3)  \nMeld 4: T4,T5,T? (need T6 for chow, only 2 unshown T6 left) or B3,B3,B3 (need 1 more B3)  \nPair: B7,B7.  \n\nSo best discard now: something not reducing possible chows/pungs.  \n\n**Most useless tile in hand:**  \n- B7: only 2 unshown left, but I might need it as pair if I get another B7.  \n- T5: many T5 left, could be used in chow T3,T4,T5 if I get T3 or T4 extra.  \n- T2: useful for chow T2,T3,T4.  \n- T3: very useful (pung/chow).  \n- T4: useful.  \n- B3: very useful for pung.  \n\nSo weakest is B7 or T5. B7 as pair needs one more B7 (2 left). T5 for chow needs T3,T4,T5, but T4 is only 1 in hand, so T5\u2019s chow possibility is low unless I draw T4 again.  \n\nGiven unshown: T4 has 4 left, so possible to get another T4, but then T3,T4,T5 chow would use both T4 tiles \u2014 but currently only 1 T4 in hand, so need to draw T4 first.  \n\nBetter to keep flexible: T5 more flexible than B7? Actually B7 only useful for pair; T5 can be part of chow if I draw T3/T4.  \n\nI think B7 is least connected to other tiles, so discard B7.  \n\n**Reason:**  \n- My hand is close to two more melds: one from T2,T3,T4 (already complete in hand), one from B3 pung (need 1 more B3) or T3 pung (need 1 more T3).  \n- Keeping all T tiles preserves chow options.  \n- Discarding B7 leaves B3\u00d72 for possible pung, and if I draw B7 again, I can keep as pair.  \n- Discarding B7 doesn\u2019t break any chow/pung chances because B7 only pairs.  \n- Unshown B7=2, so chance to pair later still possible if drawn.  \n\nFinal choice: Play B7.\n\n**Answer:** Play B7"}
